# Mobile screen layout

Use `ScreenShell`, `ScreenScroll`, and `ScreenFooter` from `@/components/screen-shell` for new full-screen routes.

## Pattern

- **`ScreenShell`** — `flex: 1` root; measures sticky footer height for scroll inset.
- **`ScreenScroll`** — vertical page scroll with tab-bar inset (tab routes) and/or footer inset (`reserveFooter`).
- **`ScreenFooter`** — absolute bottom bar; children handle safe-area `paddingBottom` (e.g. `useSafeAreaInsets()`).
- **`HorizontalRail`** — nested horizontal scroll; use `horizontalRailContentStyle()` for gutter + gap.

## Defaults

- Horizontal gutter: `SCREEN_GUTTER` (16).
- Custom top chrome (e.g. `ScreenSearchHeader`): pass `contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior="never"` on `ScreenScroll`.
- Do not hardcode large `paddingBottom` (e.g. 140) for footers — use `ScreenFooter` + `reserveFooter`.

## Tab screens

`ScreenScroll` already applies floating tab bar inset via `useFloatingTabBarContentInset`. No footer unless the screen has its own sticky actions.
